---
export const prerender = true;
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
import { Guestbook } from '../components/Guestbook';
import '../styles/components/_prose.css';
import '../styles/components/_about.css';

const links = [
  { label: 'email', href: 'mailto:hello@oddava.me' },
  { label: 'github', href: 'https://github.com/oddava' },
  { label: 'x', href: 'https://x.com/oddava' },
];
---

<Base
  title="about"
  description="how i got into code, what i'm building now, and what i'm after."
>
  <article class="about">
    <h1>about</h1>

    <p class="about__lead">hey, i'm oddava, a backend developer.</p>

    <p>
      back in high school, the first thing i ever built was a clock that lived
      in my telegram name. once a minute, a script woke up, checked the time and
      renamed me. nobody asked for it, me included. but a few lines in a file
      had a real app doing what i told it to, and there was no going back.
    </p>

    <p>
      i learned the backend properly at PDP Academy: python, django, databases,
      algorithms. the mentors were great, but most of what stuck came from my
      own projects. the biggest was AniShows, an anime tracker with watchlists,
      reviews and forums. when i found out AniList doesn't let competing
      trackers use its data, i moved the whole catalog sync to a self-hosted
      Jikan instance.
    </p>

    <p>
      now i write code for a living. work moved me from django to node.js,
      typescript and vue, and i picked them up quickly. my first big job was
      replacing an old php site without losing a single article. since then it's
      been things like tracking down session bugs that only showed up once a
      token expired.
    </p>

    <p>
      i use AI every day to move faster, find my way around unfamiliar code, and
      learn. one rule: i only ship what i understand.
    </p>

    <p>
      outside of work it's side projects, reading about new tech, and following
      developers on x (probably more than i should).
    </p>

    <p>
      i'm early in my career and i know it. next, i want to work with people
      better than me, keep improving, and build things people actually use.
    </p>

    <p>
      this site is where i keep my <a href="/notes">notes</a> and anything else worth
      remembering.
    </p>

    <footer class="about__contact">
      <h2 class="about__label">say hi</h2>
      <ul class="about__links">
        {
          links.map((link) => {
            const isExternal = link.href.startsWith('http');
            return (
              <li>
                <a
                  href={link.href}
                  target={isExternal ? '_blank' : undefined}
                  rel={isExternal ? 'noopener noreferrer' : undefined}
                  aria-label={
                    isExternal ? `${link.label} (opens in new tab)` : undefined
                  }
                >
                  {link.label}
                </a>
              </li>
            );
          })
        }
      </ul>
    </footer>
  </article>

  <Guestbook client:idle />
  <noscript>
    <p class="guestbook-noscript">
      the guestbook needs javascript to load and post notes. with it off, you
      can still say hi at <a href="mailto:hello@oddava.me">hello@oddava.me</a>.
    </p>
  </noscript>
</Base>
